  "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)=5sin\u2061(2x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13939267/assets/67f6ec4f72e7bd74ac9ae5fa0f195cda1e90e8d8e6fad1bf85944a3dfd17fdfb.png)\n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty $, the graph oscillates between the values $y=-5$ and $y=5$ indefinitely. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)={lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }5sin\u2061(2x)=DNE.\n$$",
